# Crypto/package test fixtures (keys, signed artifacts, .hart archives, hash
# test inputs, etc.) must be checked out byte-for-byte identical on every
# platform. Several unit tests hash or sign/verify this content, so even
# newline normalization (e.g. LF -> CRLF, applied by git's autocrlf on some
# Windows runners/images) silently changes the fixture bytes and breaks the
# tests with "hash doesn't match" failures. Mark the whole tree binary so git
# never performs end-of-line conversion on it, regardless of autocrlf config.
components/core/tests/fixtures/** -text
